TEXT -1016 168 Left 2 !*\n.param Gfc=10 ; gain (in dB) you want a crossover\n.param fc=1k ; targeted crossover\n.param  G=(10**(Gfc/20))\n*\n* Capture the double zero position and one of the pole position *\n*\n.param  R1=22k ; R1 is arbitrarily selected\n.param  fz1=200\n.param  fz2=600\n.param  fp1=6k ; this is the PID pole in the filtered version\n*\n* Do not edit the below lines *\n*\n.param  wz1={2*pi*fz1}\n.param  wz2={2*pi*fz2}\n.param  wp1={2*pi*fp1}\n*\n*\n.param  j={(1+fz1**2/fc**2)*(1+fc**2/fz2**2)}\n.param  G0={G*sqrt((1+fc**2/fp1**2)/j)}\n.param  Wpi={wz1*G0}\n.param  z={(Wp1-Wz1)*(Wp1-Wz2)}\n.param  f={Wp1*Wz1+Wp1*Wz2-Wz1*Wz2}\n*\n.param  Td={z/(f*Wp1)}\n.param  N={((Wp1**2)/f)-1}\n.param  kp={(Wpi/Wz1)-(Wpi/Wp1)+(Wpi/Wz2)}\n.param  Ti={((Wz1+Wz2)/(Wz1*Wz2))-(1/Wp1)}\n.param  ki={kp/Ti}\n.param  kd={kp*Td}\n*\n.param  A={sqrt(N**2*Ti**2-4*N**2*Td*Ti-2*N*Td*Ti+Td**2)}\n.param  C1={(Td+A+N*Ti)/(2*N*R1)}\n.param  CD={kp*Td*(1+N)*(2*Ti*N**2+Ti*N+A-Td)/(2*N**3*R1*Ti)}\n.param  R2={R1/(kp+N*kp)}\n.param  RD={R1*(N*Ti-Td-A)/(2*kp*Td*(1+N))}\n*
TEXT -64 32 Left 2 !.ac dec 100 10 100k
TEXT 96 624 Left 2 ;This a classical PID - 1 pole at the origin, 2 zeroes
TEXT 104 896 Left 2 ;This a filtered PID - 1 pole at the origin, 2 zeroes, 1 pole
TEXT 104 1168 Left 2 ;This a type 3a - 1 pole at the origin, 2 zeroes, 1 pole
